message: "If you use this dossier or its analytical frameworks, cite this publication."
title: "Teaching the Names and Artificial Intelligence: What Does the Evidence Establish About Machine Understanding?"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Alhafiz
    given-names: Ahmed
    affiliation: Independent author and researcher
version: "2.0"
date-released: 2026-09-02
url: "https://ahmed-alhafiz.github.io/articles/teaching-names-ai-understanding/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ahmed-Alhafiz/ahmed-alhafiz.github.io"
abstract: >-
  A bilingual evidence-led dossier separating six layers often compressed
  into the word understanding: symbol discrimination, distributional
  association, compositional transfer, grounded reference, causal and
  interventional modelling, and intention, experience and responsibility.
  The dossier proposes a Six-Layer Understanding Matrix and a 6x4 testing
  protocol as explicitly non-validated analytical syntheses.
keywords:
  - language models
  - machine understanding
  - symbol grounding
  - semantic representation
  - multimodal grounding
  - causal reasoning
  - artificial consciousness
  - teaching the names
  - Quran and artificial intelligence
